      "lem:score-diffuseness"
    ],
    "justification": "The frontier weighted-Lindeberg bounds must adapt to both the treated-pre and donor-window variance components as \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) vary.",
    "gap": "No checked weak-factor result derives score diffuseness uniformly over a three-exponent deterministic block-missing class.",
    "consumer": "The frontier central limit theorem uses these bounds without fixing the cohort exponent at one.",
    "proof_tex": "The normalized-factor argument in the proof of \\(\\mathrm{lem:score\\mbox{-}diffuseness}\\) uses only balanced growth, incoherence, and the two restricted-Gram bounds.  It therefore gives uniformly on every compact exponent set\n\\[\n |a_{ij,t}|\\le Cn^{-1},\n \\qquad |b_{t,s}|\\le Cn^{-1}.\n\\]\nWith \\(g\\asymp n^b\\) and \\(H\\asymp n^c\\), expansion of the three-term score gives\n\\[\n \\max_{j,s'}|w_{js'}|\n \\le C\\max\\left\\{\\frac1{nH},\\frac1{ng},\\frac1{n^2}\\right\\}\n\\]\nand, by counting the same three disjoint supports,\n\\[\n \\sum_{j,s'}w_{js'}^2\n \\le C\\left\\{\\frac1{nH}+\\frac1{ng}+\\frac1{n^2}\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThe frontier variance lower bound is\n\\[\n s^2\\ge c_v\\left\\{\\frac1{nH}+\\frac1{ng}\\right\\},\n\\]\nso the squared-weight sum divided by \\(s^2\\) is uniformly bounded.  Each component of the maximum is negligible relative to \\(s\\):\n\\[\n \\frac{(nH)^{-1}}{s}\\le\\frac1{\\sqrt{nH}},\n \\qquad\n \\frac{(ng)^{-1}}{s}\\le\\frac1{\\sqrt{ng}},\n \\qquad\n \\frac{n^{-2}}{s}\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{nH}}{n^2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{ng}}{n^2}.\n\\]\nOn a compact subset of \\([1/2,1]\\times(0,1]\\times[0,1]\\), the exponent \\(b\\) is bounded below by a positive constant, while \\(c\\ge0\\).  Thus \\(nH\\to\\infty\\), \\(ng\\to\\infty\\), and every right-hand side tends to zero uniformly.  This proves the frontier diffuseness claims.",
